    "id": "train-3718",
    "question": "Tom opens an amusement park.  It cost $100,000 to open initially.  It also cost 1% of that to run per day.  He sells 150  tickets a day for $10 each.  How long will it take to make back his money?",
    "gold": "200",
    "answer": "It cost 100,000*.01=$<<100000*.01=1000>>1,000 a day to keep the place open\nHe makes 150*10=$<<150*10=1500>>1500 a day from the park\nSo he makes a profit of 1500-1000=$<<1500-1000=500>>500 a day\nSo it takes 100000/500=<<100000/500=200>>200 days to make back his money\n#### 200"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how long it will take Tom to make back his initial investment, we need to calculate his daily profit and then find out how many days it will take to cover the initial cost of $100,000.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the daily cost to run the amusement park. The daily cost is 1% of the initial cost of $100,000:\n\\[\n\\text{Daily cost} = 0.01 \\times 100,000 = 1,000\n\\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the daily revenue from ticket sales. Tom sells 150 tickets a day at $10 each:\n\\[\n\\text{Daily revenue} = 150 \\times 10 = 1,500\n\\]\n\nNow, we can find the daily profit by subtracting the daily cost from the daily revenue:\n\\[\n\\text{Daily profit} = \\text{Daily revenue} - \\text{Daily cost} = 1,500 - 1,000 = 500\n\\]\n\nTo find out how many days it will take to make back the initial investment of $100,000, we divide the initial investment by the daily profit:\n\\[\n\\text{Number of days} = \\frac{100,000}{500} = 200\n\\]\n\nTherefore, it will take Tom \\(\\boxed{200}\\) days to make back his money.",
